comments.body:
@participant6 Have you encountered any more timeouts or other issues with Exasol tests?

@reporter 
We are almost certain that the timeouts were caused by the database not coming up correctly due to hard disk pressure on the github runner. Our latest PR related to tests did, in all probability, fix this issue by providing a way slimmer Exasol dockerdb image.

So, while not strictly necessary, this PR should be an improvement: 
In case of any issue with the database not correctly starting the new timeout guards will make the CI fail within minutes instead of hours.
The new waiting strategy is something that's also used at Exasol in-house ( and is the proper waiting strategy to make sure the database is up and working correctly ).
